 you might see me  juggling with all of the different  pieces to get like pieces around it the  sort of dome the glass is that it's just  a very very narrow sort of window II  roof and I can't really sink any walls  into that because I know it'll look  really awkward from the interior of the  station so hence why it's also kind of  hard sometimes to add things around the  station Mariya the backside is used one  copy of the front sort of entrance arch  with a small roof with a little test  sort of dormer which I figured it will  it should be quite nice to use the bells  which are only possible if you really  have a wall to sink them into to get  some of those iron accents to at least  get a bit more of that industrial  steampunky feeling into the station  another thing actually which is you  might have noticed in this video is that  I got some new music I try to get new  music for every single series that I get  and try to sort of fit it with the theme  it is kind of hard to exactly do that  with steampunk since what mostly defines  steampunk music as a sub-genre is just  that it's part of these steampunk  community if you will and it has sort of  steampunk acts around it but I really  figured some of that other electro-swing  though mostly some really old sort of  turn of the 20th century kind of break  beats and trip-hop music is just what I  really like personally and works quite  well for the theme I think since it has  that mixture of the the old and the new  and that really well Industrial feeling  to it as well now I skipped a section of  the time I'm here or rather I forgot to  time-lapse that parts actually forgot to  record it so I'm sorry about that all I  did in that small section though was  just add some parts which turned out to  be a real hassle so maybe better that I  didn't record it because there was a lot  of trial and error to get them  the way I wanted them to and just add a  few rocks and some simple foliage and a  simple black fence around the coaster at  this point I also try to make a chimney  which will definitely come back at some  point in the future but not something  that I want to have around this part and  especially not something I want to have  around this station because this station  is more or less going to be a wienie as  you want to enter the at the ride and  definitely want to keep the station the  tallest building within its sort of  general surroundings to make that really  what draws your attention around here  and I figured one way to get some simple  scenery because every single thing that  I make I'm somehow gonna make somehow  gonna have to make all of the different  pieces into industrial looking things  and I figured a guess summer would  actually work quite well if that is  actually how you pronounce it over here  which is one of those like old gas  storage tanks which rise up and go down  during the day which they used to build  at the end of the 19th century I think  it also has a sort of factory look to it  and it's one more excuse to get some  pipelines and pipe works in general  machinery around this area and I  definitely do want to fill up the area  around the station a bit more but I'm  really gonna have to find out it's how  to give every single part of the ride  its own sort of useless contraption and  machinery  kind of look to it anyway that's about  it for the time lapse for today I do  have some real life shots or real time  shots I should say just to show it off a  little bit better than what you see in  the time-lapse this is basically what  the station looks like from the front  although not directly from the front it  it's just that I find I usually just  make buildings in a way that they're  meant to be viewed from one sort of  particular place not that they would  look bad from other places but generally  kind of build a building from one place  and that last shot was definitely sort  of the best here to view the building  from I think and what I sort of  intention intended it to be seen from  the front is definitely pretty important  to them where it really resembles the  Disneyland station quite a bit even  though it has all sorts of different  detail  and some different general shapes it  still has these sort of standing to  towers and the interior is really  similar to an old train station with all  of the pillars and the arches on the  roof and things like that  I might put some more scenery in there  actually and then the building from a  sort of top-down perspective basically  looks like this it's actually not that  big of a building and looks a bit larger  than it really is because of the force  perspective of being the being placed on  a hill but that's all just kind of parts  of the idea of the ride it's going to be  quite a small ride but I'll try to make  it look bit larger than it really should  anyway that is really about it for today  so thank you guys for watching and I  hope to see you guys next time
 

